 "result_text": "You can now pick which sound a chime plays. `play_speaker` in `api.py` and `Chime.play` in `devices.py` take two new optional arguments, `ringtone_id` and `track_no`. The `chimes play` CLI command has matching `--ringtone-id` and `-t`/`--track-no` options. I haven't run any tests or tried it against a real chime.\n\n- **Request:** the API call sends the chosen sound along with volume and repeat count. Any value you leave out falls back to the chime's current setting, except `ringtone_id`, which is only sent when you give one.\n- **Untested guess:** I assumed the play-speaker endpoint accepts a `ringtoneId` field, since the repo doesn't show the payload for custom sounds. If uploaded sounds need a different field, that part will need adjusting.\n- **Behaviour change:** passing only `track_no` or `ringtone_id` (no volume or repeat) now sends a request body. Before, a plain play sent none.",
